acturer","conflict":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://docs.mech-mind.net/en/eye-3d-camera/latest/hardware/camera-models.html","title":"Camera Selection Guide","date":null,"quote":"ULTRA M-V5D2000A 1800 1300–2200 ±2"}],"formatted":"1300–2200 mm"},{"metric":"release_date","label":"Release date","group":"Hardware","value":"2026-08-12","unit":"","conditions":"Configuration: Official product launch announcement; earlier 2026 demonstrations were previews","claimStage":"unknown","controlMode":"unknown","evidenceKind":"manufacturer","conflict":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.mech-mind.com/news/the-new-mech-eye-ultra-m-gl.html","title":"The New Mech-Eye ULTRA M-GL Redefines 3D Vision for Sub-1 mm Thin Parts, Transparent Objects, and High-Speed Robotics | Mech-Mind Robotics","date":null,"quote":"08/12/2026 High-quality industrial 3D vision enables robots to accurately perceive, understand, and interact with the physical world. Yet real-world manufacturing and logistics environments continue to present major challenges for robot vision. Sub-1 mm thin parts and transparent materials are difficult to reconstruct reliably with industrial 3D cameras, while increasingly demanding cycle times leave little room for lengthy image acquisition. To address these challenges, Mech-Mind launches Mech-Eye ULTRA M-GL, its flagship industrial 3D camera with high resolution and high speed as well as the latest addition to the company's embodied AI “Eye-Brain-Hand” portfolio."}],"formatted":"2026-08-12"},{"metric":"resolution","label":"Resolution","group":"Hardware","value":"Depth Map： 2448 × 2048 RGB： 4000 x 3000 2000 x 1500","unit":"","conditions":"Configuration: ULTRA M-GL catalog column","claimStage":"unknown","controlMode":"unknown","evidenceKind":"manufacturer","conflict":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.mech-mind.com/products/mech-eye-industrial-3d-camera.html","title":"Mech-Mind Robotics — robotics component scope","date":null,"quote":"Resolution 2048 × 1536 1280 × 1024 2400 × 18